q155 = d.move(p155, n3)
d.replace(q155, 'At equal molar distalization (Table 3, Fig. 3), the molar crown had tipped more in the headgear group (0.94 ± 0.04 mm) than in any aligner group (0.73–0.77 mm; Holm p = 0.013, all patients), and its root apex had moved mesially (−0.14 ± 0.04 mm) rather than distally. The first molar was extruded (−0.22 ± 0.04 mm), more than in the PC group in every patient (p = 0.021) and more than in the hook groups in four of five patients, and its distobuccal cusp had moved 0.61 ± 0.48 mm palatally (Friedman p = 0.004). The canine had moved 0.12 ± 0.13 mm distally with headgear but 0.12–0.17 mm mesially with the aligner designs and 0.36 mm mesially in the control (Friedman p = 0.002). Incisor retraction and incisor vertical movement did not differ between groups at this point (p = 0.095); because the aligners had not yet activated the anterior teeth, these values reflect anchorage loss rather than planned retraction.')
f3 = d.move(fig3_img, q155)
l3 = d.move(fig3_leg, f3)
d.replace(l3, '**Fig. 3 Tooth displacement at equal first-molar distalization (primary analysis).** Displacement at the moment the mesiobuccal cusp of the first molar had moved 0.8 mm distally: a distal crown tipping of the first molar (crown minus apex sagittal displacement); b first-molar vertical movement; c transverse movement of the first-molar distobuccal cusp; d canine distalization; e canine vertical movement; f incisor retraction; g incisor vertical movement. Dots are individual patients and bars are means. Positive values indicate distal, buccal or intrusive movement; for the incisor, positive retraction is palatal. HG, fixed appliance with cervical headgear; PC, precision cut; CAH, aligner-material hook; CMH, bonded metal hook; Ctrl, aligner without elastics.')
pth = body('The comparison was repeated at thresholds from 0.4 to 1.2 mm (every group reached at least 1.27 mm in every patient) and along the whole distalization path (Fig. 4; Additional file 2). The greater molar extrusion with headgear than with the precision cut, the palatal displacement of the distobuccal cusp with headgear, the more distal canine position with headgear and every difference between the precision cut and the hooks kept their sign at every threshold. The greater molar tipping and the mesial root-apex movement with headgear were present from 0.6 mm onwards but reversed at about 0.2–0.4 mm, and the canine vertical and incisor sagittal differences between headgear and aligners changed sign between 0.6 and 1.0 mm.')
f4 = d.new_figure(fig_tmpl, os.path.join(SP, 'figs', 'Fig_trajectory_matched.png'))
l4 = legend('**Fig. 4 Tooth displacement as a function of first-molar distalization.** Each outcome is plotted against the distal movement of the mesiobuccal cusp of the first molar from 0 to 1.25 mm (mean of five patients; shaded bands, ±1 SD for HG and PC). The dotted line marks the 0.8-mm primary comparison point. Panel titles give the landmark and sign convention. HG, fixed appliance with cervical headgear; PC, precision cut; CAH, aligner-material hook; CMH, bonded metal hook; Control, aligner without elastics.')
