hv = body('**Headgear force systems. **Table 6 compares the main headgear model with the three alternative force systems. Pointing the force along the elastic direction of each patient turned the extrusion of the first molar into intrusion (1.06 ± 0.25 mm at the end of the protocol), reduced canine extrusion from 2.09 to 1.36 mm and the palatal displacement of the distobuccal cusp from 4.71 to 2.48 mm, but increased distal crown tipping from 2.28 to 4.13 mm. Passing the cervical force through the centroid of the first molar reduced the palatal displacement of the distobuccal cusp to 1.04 ± 0.44 mm, canine extrusion to 0.93 ± 0.13 mm and incisor extrusion to 0.63 ± 0.08 mm, and at equal distalization it removed the extra molar tipping (0.78 ± 0.06 mm). The levelled set-up changed the results little. Under all three variants, the headgear-versus-precision-cut differences at equal molar distalization in molar extrusion, palatal displacement of the distobuccal cusp and canine distalization kept their sign in at least four of five patients, whereas the canine vertical difference reversed with the matched force direction (Additional file 2).')
